# MCProuter Development Guide

MCProuter is a reverse proxy/router for horizontally scaled MCP (Model Context Protocol) servers in Kubernetes environments.

## Project Overview

This project implements a cloud-native solution for scaling MCP servers horizontally in Kubernetes, solving the core issue of session affinity in MCP's 1:1 client-to-server relationship model.

### Key Architecture Components

- **Session Affinity**: Maintains consistent routing of client sessions to backend servers
- **Streamable HTTP Transport**: Uses HTTP-only subset (no SSE streaming) of the 2025-03-26 specification
- **Consistent Hashing**: Enables horizontal scaling of MCProuter instances
- **Kubernetes Service Discovery**: Dynamically discovers MCP server pods via K8s API
- **Load Balancing**: Intelligent distribution of client sessions across available backends

